; Declaration-position syntax/for OUTSIDE any macro template: refused
; (AX3028) and re-tagged inert, so the checker walks a well-formed
; list. `.axbad` because the formatter must not learn the shape - a
; top-level syntax/for prints through the expression printer, which
; rewrites its interior `fn` forms - so committing it as `.ax` would
; bake a different tree.
(struct P (x : Int))

(syntax/for (f (syntax/fields P))
  (fn (g) 1))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main) 0)
